=== Generated Answer (model draft; check against evidence) ===
No — they use more than the tweets themselves; they also build graphs from tweet mentions and use Twitter/social-media features to detect troll roles.

The paper's dataset is tweets by IRA-linked users (2,973,371 tweets by 2,848 Twitter users) [10], but their method extracts features from social media (Twitter) beyond raw tweet text [6]. In particular, they build a User-to-Mentioned-User (U2M) graph where an edge exists if one user mentions another in a tweet, and they run node2vec on it to extract user embeddings [2]. They use node2vec because they lack access to user attributes, having only the tweets from the "IRA Russian Trolls" dataset [1].
